{"id": "life-generations-cash-to-iou", "title": "Cash fell $307.6 million at 27 Life Generations nursing homes", "seconds": 130.1, "voice": "elevenlabs:9PVP7ENhDskL0KYHAKtD", "narrator": "Jerry B.", "tempo": 1.079, "made": "2026-11-25", "key": "277976e93aa5b6d8", "words": 430, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "timeline[0]", "trajectory"], "text": "314.2 million dollars.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 2.55, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$314.2 million", "label": "cash and securities, 27 California nursing homes", "sub": "end of 2024"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.23, 0.51, 1.0, 1.26, 1.57, 1.93]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "timeline[0]"], "text": "That was cash and securities on the filed opening balance sheets for 27 California nursing homes.", "t0": 2.67, "t1": 7.25, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$314.2 million", "label": "cash and securities, 27 California nursing homes", "sub": "end of 2024"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.28, 0.57, 0.68, 1.22, 1.31, 1.42, 1.74, 2.06, 2.38, 2.61, 2.75, 3.35, 3.92, 4.24]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "timeline[1]", "amount"], "text": "A year later, 6.6 million remained. The decline was 307.6 million dollars.", "t0": 7.37, "t1": 13.06, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$6.6 million", "label": "the same 27 homes, end of 2025", "sub": "$307.6 million decline in cash and securities"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.37, 0.94, 1.23, 1.52, 1.81, 2.13, 2.94, 3.09, 3.53, 3.67, 3.91, 4.24, 4.53, 4.79, 5.03, 5.33]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "caveat", "ref": ["caveat"], "text": "It’s a lead, not a finding.", "t0": 13.68, "t1": 14.94, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "caveat", "line": "This is a lead, not a finding: a pattern in public records. This film says what the records show, what they do not show, and what would settle it."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.3, 0.61, 0.77, 0.84]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "caveat", "ref": ["innocent[0]", "status"], "text": "Pooling cash with a parent company is common, and the homes still count it as theirs.", "t0": 15.06, "t1": 19.07, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "caveat", "line": "This is a lead, not a finding: a pattern in public records. This film says what the records show, what they do not show, and what would settle it."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.37, 0.67, 0.81, 0.87, 1.16, 1.54, 1.66, 2.25, 2.46, 2.57, 2.85, 3.12, 3.36, 3.47, 3.58]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "actors[0]", "links[1]"], "text": "The first lead. All 27 homes name one parent: Life Generations Healthcare.", "t0": 19.29, "t1": 23.82, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Life Generations Healthcare", "kicker": "The first lead", "sub": "the parent named by 27 homes", "chip": "8 in the Bay Area, 1 in San Francisco"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.41, 1.03, 1.26, 1.81, 2.09, 2.32, 2.5, 3.18, 3.43, 4.04]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "links[0]"], "text": "As the cash went, what related companies owed the homes rose to 298.8 million.", "t0": 23.94, "t1": 28.84, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["cash, end of 2025", "$6.6 million"], "b": ["owed to the homes by related companies", "$298.8 million"]}, "emph": ["298.8 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.3, 0.6, 1.06, 1.27, 1.63, 2.08, 2.25, 2.36, 2.69, 2.92, 3.04, 3.28, 3.6, 4.07, 4.32, 4.52]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[0]"], "text": "The homes’ net income that year: 53.6 million.", "t0": 28.96, "t1": 32.08, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["cash, end of 2025", "$6.6 million"], "b": ["owed to the homes by related companies", "$298.8 million"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.43, 0.62, 0.93, 1.11, 1.61, 2.2, 2.48, 2.76]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "established[3]", "innocent[5]"], "text": "Of the 335.1 million swing, 239.4 million was the increase in amounts owed to homes.", 