", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "no State enforcement action at the four Bay Area homes", "kicker": "Cal Health Find, 2025"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.26, 0.55, 0.79, 0.94, 1.43, 1.72, 1.83, 1.96, 2.21, 2.29, 2.56]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "form", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[1]"], "text": "The third lead: the lines for owners’ draws, dividends and transfers are blank in every report.", "t0": 76.24, "t1": 81.02, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "form", "title": "The equity page, every 2025 report", "rows": [["Owners’ draws", "blank"], ["Dividends", "blank"], ["Related-party transfers", "blank"]]}, "emph": ["blank"], "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.43, 0.95, 1.12, 1.41, 1.57, 1.88, 2.5, 2.96, 3.05, 3.59, 3.72, 4.02, 4.13, 4.37]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "established[2]"], "text": "Yet the homes did pay related companies: 6.2 million to Theragen, for therapy.", "t0": 81.14, "t1": 85.54, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Paid to related companies by the group’s homes, 2025", "rows": [["Theragen, therapy services", "$6.2 million"], ["Life Generations Healthcare, management fees", "$4.5 million"], ["Real Estate Entity 3, building lease", "$2.4 million"], ["Real Estate - San Jose Note, building lease", "$884,837"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.29, 0.62, 0.85, 1.08, 1.43, 2.14, 2.4, 2.64, 2.85, 3.16, 3.24, 3.77, 3.95]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "established[2]"], "text": "4.5 million in management fees, and building leases to related landlords.", "t0": 85.66, "t1": 89.55, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Paid to related companies by the group’s homes, 2025", "rows": [["Theragen, therapy services", "$6.2 million"], ["Life Generations Healthcare, management fees", "$4.5 million"], ["Real Estate Entity 3, building lease", "$2.4 million"], ["Real Estate - San Jose Note, building lease", "$884,837"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.23, 0.48, 0.78, 1.07, 1.16, 1.56, 2.01, 2.21, 2.54, 2.85, 2.99, 3.37]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "actors[3]"], "text": "The fourth lead is in San Francisco: Lawton Skilled Nursing and Rehabilitation Center.", "t0": 89.77, "t1": 93.85, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "Lawton Skilled Nursing & Rehabilitation Center", "kicker": "The fourth lead", "sub": "San Francisco"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.4, 0.6, 0.72, 0.82, 1.03, 1.97, 2.3, 2.64, 2.95, 3.06, 3.76]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what", "links[3]"], "text": "Its cash fell from 9.1 million to 218,549 dollars.", "t0": 93.97, "t1": 98.83, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$218,549", "label": "Lawton’s cash, end of 2025", "sub": "from $9.1 million"}, "emph": ["218,549"], "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.48, 0.68, 0.85, 1.08, 1.35, 1.54, 1.97, 2.16, 2.35, 2.6, 3.0, 3.41, 3.68, 3.94, 4.45]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what", "suspicious[3].why", "innocent[5]"], "text": "Lawton owed related companies 11.2 million. A year later, it owed 2.7 million.", "t0": 98.95, "t1": 104.35, "shot": "b16b", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Lawton owed related companies, end of 2024", "$11.2 million"], "b": ["still owed, end of 2025", "$2.7 million"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.37, 0.51, 0.86, 1.29, 1.66, 1.91, 2.13, 2.94, 3.1, 3.32, 3.85, 4.01, 4.19, 4.42, 4.72, 5.04]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what"], "text": "The federal ownership file lists 5 organizations with a role in it now, against 1 in 2019.", "t0": 104.47, "t1": 109.68, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["organizations with a role in the home, 2019", "1"], "b": ["2026", "5"], "kicker": "Federal ownership file", "arrows": false}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.42, 0.86, 1.15, 1.4, 1.67, 2.3, 2.44, 2.52, 2.75, 2.86, 2.97, 3.61, 4.02, 4.27, 4.37, 4.68]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[1]", "notEstablished[2]"], "text": "The records don’t show where the cash went, or whether it can be repaid.", "t0": 109.9, "t1": 113.32, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["Where the cash went", "Whether it can be repaid, or carries interest", "Whether any of it reached the owners"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.49, 0.72, 0.93, 1.08, 1.18, 1.52, 2.1, 2.3, 2.57, 2.66, 2.8, 2.93]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[2]"], "text": "Or whether any of it reached the owners.", "t0": 113.44, "t1": 115.02, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["Where the cash went", "Whether it can be repaid, or carries interest", "Whether any of it reached the owners"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.44, 0.62, 0.73, 0.84, 1.08, 1.23]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["innocent[0]", "innocent[2]"], "text": "A central treasury or a loan agreement could explain it, and the 2025 reports aren’t audited.", "t0": 115.14, "t1": 119.73, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "The 2025 reports are as submitted, not audited."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.44, 0.86, 0.97, 1.04, 1.23, 1.59, 1.75, 2.15, 2.49, 2.67, 2.78, 3.07, 3.62, 4.0, 4.24]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[1]"], "text": "What would settle it? The group’s audited statements, its cash agreement, and the State’s own audit.", "t0": 119.85, "t1": 124.59, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "Life Generations Healthcare", "what": "audited 2025 statements and cash-management agreement"}, {"who": "The State", "what": "its audit of the 2025 reports"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.34, 0.64, 1.09, 1.24, 1.53, 1.87, 2.44, 2.66, 2.95, 3.5, 3.75, 3.86, 4.27, 4.48]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status", "defense[0]"], "text": "No authority has made a finding about these homes.", "t0": 124.71, "t1": 126.95, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.62, 0.75, 0.92, 1.01, 1.38, 1.61, 1.82]}, {"scene": "close"